WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.030
- In all seriousness, let's talk

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.980
about what you want to
accomplish as a first lady.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.840
I know education is
really important to you.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:05.673
- Very important.

00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:06.853
- Why you're my favorite.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:09.360
And I grew up with an educator for a mama

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.390
and y'all work so hard, so tirelessly

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.640
and sometimes it's a very thankless job.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.450
And so I know that education is important.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.272
I know military is very important to you

00:00:18.272 --> 00:00:19.267
- Yes.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.440
personally, and anything else like

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.580
you're really wanting to focus on

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.040
- You know, I, I am fighting
for free community college.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.080
I've been doing that

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.670
since we were in the Obama
Biden administration.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.830
I mean, it's very important

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.250
to me and my students and, and
I've been fighting, you know

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.370
to change the face of
cancer as we know it.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.260
I don't think there's one American family

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.830
that hasn't been touched by cancer

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.350
and it's not a Republican
thing or a Democrat thing.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.280
It's a, it's a human issue.
It's an American issue.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.152
We must get cancer under control.

00:00:50.152 --> 00:00:52.050
And then right now I'm
focused on, you know

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.560
getting this pandemic under control.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.393
- Amen.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.320
- Before we do anything, we, you know, we

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.890
we have so much to do, but
we have to get the pandemic

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.910
under control and get,
you know, people back

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:10.210
to work and kids back in
schools and we have to

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.980
get people vaccinated
and Joe's working so hard

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:16.520
to get everybody in this
country vaccinated so.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.370
- Yeah, we can get back
to some kind of normal

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:19.310
- [First Lady] Yes.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:22.680
- I just would personally love
to just go to a dinner party.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.513
- Ya!

00:01:23.513 --> 00:01:25.810
- Like, I mean, my kid now
just got back in school

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.410
physically but I was just like, Whoa,

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.970
I can't wait for that to end but you,

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.250
this is one thing I love about you,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.970
You're, you still keep your job.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:35.286
- I do.

00:01:35.286 --> 00:01:37.420
- Cause you still work
in community college

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.870
and you're also the first lady.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.260
That's a lot of, as a woman
that loves to be busy myself.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.020
How do you find balance, especially

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.130
with a family involved in that as well?

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.320
- Well, you know, I think,
I feel like I'm just

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:51.950
like you're saying, every
American woman who's working

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.900
and try to take care of a family and yeah

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.171
I love my teaching job.

00:01:57.171 --> 00:01:59.210
And then I have everything
in all the issues

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.510
that I'm working on in the white house.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:04.610
So it's like every other
American women woman.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.100
And I think, you know, moms have had it.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.000
I mean, they were struggling
before the pandemic

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.550
and I think it's just really
exacerbated everything

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.950
that moms have to handle.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.913
And now they're helping their kids online.

00:02:19.296 --> 00:02:20.310
And, and by the way

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.500
haven't our teachers been so amazing,

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.923
I just love, love love our teachers.

00:02:25.923 --> 00:02:27.595
(applause)

00:02:27.595 --> 00:02:29.600
- Shout out to my kids school because it's

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.675
it's a hard thing because
teaching isn't, I mean, you go

00:02:32.675 --> 00:02:34.475
to school to learn how
to be a great teacher

00:02:34.475 --> 00:02:36.180
and it is a gift innately
given I think not

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.710
everyone is great at teaching.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:40.410
So it's an incredible thing
that I think people now realize.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.362
I've been shouting it for years just

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.195
- Thank you.

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:44.882
- Because I have a spotlight
and my mom was a teacher.

00:02:44.882 --> 00:02:46.503
Well, and it's, it's really important.

00:02:46.503 --> 00:02:48.320
And I think people are
just now, unfortunately

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.300
a silver lining from
this whole situation has

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.350
been realizing how hard
it is to be a teacher.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.530
People are like, Oh, I have
to wrangle my three kids.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.460
I'm like, teachers have
to wrangle like 25 to 30.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.346
I'm like, I'm, it's a hard job.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.179
- Yeah.

00:03:01.179 --> 00:03:04.330
- And I, I love that one time
you spoke about, you know, in

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.034
in your sessions, cause you
do a lot over zoom, right?

00:03:07.034 --> 00:03:07.936
- [First Lady] Uh-huh.

00:03:07.936 --> 00:03:09.164
- Everybody's doing over zoom

00:03:09.164 --> 00:03:09.997
and you're sitting there
teaching your class

00:03:09.997 --> 00:03:11.910
and you have mothers that have their kids

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.300
like crawling on them or their babies.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.788
- Oh ya, oh ya.

00:03:14.788 --> 00:03:16.739
And they have nowhere to
put them, it's a hard thing.

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:17.572
- And so that's why you say like, COVID

00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:18.910
it'd be nice if we figured this out.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.619
Cause it was already hard
enough to begin with.

00:03:21.619 --> 00:03:22.452
- Yes. It was already hard enough.

00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:24.690
You know, I see from my
students, I mean, they're

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.630
you know, and I'm the one thing I have to

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.810
say is there is hope there is hope coming.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.110
I mean, we're, we're gonna
do better with childcare.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.150
We're going to get jobs.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.920
We're going to get our
kids back in schools.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.960
We're going to do better
with food insecurity.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.800
I mean, there is hope so
that's why I think I hear

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.340
that from so many people
who are saying Jill

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:46.650
we now feel like we can sort
of breathe a little bit.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.878
You know, we see the light
at the end of the tunnel

00:03:49.878 --> 00:03:52.350
and I think that's so
important for all Americans.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.610
- I agree. We need that.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.353
I cling to it sometimes, as a parent.

